      "text": "本当に申し訳ないのですが、私はあなたの傘をなくしたらしいのです。\nThis sentence sounds awkward. \nI would say \"なくしたようです\" instead of \"なくしたらしいのです.\"",
      "html": "本当に申し訳ないのですが、私はあなたの傘をなくしたらしいのです。<br/>This sentence sounds awkward. <br/>I would say \"なくしたようです\" instead of \"なくしたらしいのです.\"",
      "credits_raw": "Nick",
      "content_sha256": "413b4cf98f157f910d812670019b55eeb1f79145e93c21f8cc609f6b0ada47fc",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Some people would say \"なくしたらしい（のです）。\".",
      "html": "Some people would say \"なくしたらしい（のです）。\".",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "ec581d5f6f3cf40527dd78e3689fc00255ca559b309c6b60df5ef3a3b95871ac",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Could someone tell me what's the difference between \"Demo, Keredomo\" and \"Ga\"?",
      "html": "Could someone tell me what's the difference between \"Demo, Keredomo\" and \"Ga\"?",
      "credits_raw": "Kasomi",
      "content_sha256": "c8bfcb30c93cc603961e82d3d86ac33dcf951f67c4d754e5510b50620a1cfd84",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "as far as i know, ga is more like a \"yet\" type of but. demo means something closer to \"however\". And keredemo is closer to \"nevertheless\".",
      "html": "as far as i know, ga is more like a \"yet\" type of but. demo means something closer to \"however\". And keredemo is closer to \"nevertheless\".",
      "credits_raw": "nellyaudrey",
      "content_sha256": "f6798de4fc7b40501a28d1c350c8df942b5d48bf61aa975c6b11c16aa596eba0",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "oh, i should add that ga typically contrasts between two differing sentences. Like that one above, \n毎日一生懸命に英語を勉強したが、あまり身につかなかった。 \nI studied English very hard every day, but I did not learn a lot. \n\na demo sentence would be\nこの本はすてきでも買えないだからすぎる高いですよ．\na keredemo sentece implies that you've done something despite something else. It would be\nこの本は高いけれでも買いました．\n\nFeel free to correct any of my mistakes but these are the rules as i learned them.",
      "html": "oh, i should add that ga typically contrasts between two differing sentences. Like that one above, <br/>毎日一生懸命に英語を勉強したが、あまり身につかなかった。 <br/>I studied English very hard every day, but I did not learn a lot. <br/><br/>a demo sentence would be<br/>この本はすてきでも買えないだからすぎる高いですよ．<br/>a keredemo sentece implies that you've done something despite something else. It would be<br/>この本は高いけれでも買いました．<br/><br/>Feel free to correct any of my mistakes but these are the rules as i learned them.",
      "credits_raw": "nellyaudrey",
      "content_sha256": "5535fb09be78f6fbfadfa9a2e7eecfb61970bd013fa833ca1508d461e67b8709",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "remember, this GA is not the logic particle GA. THIS ONE comes after a VERB, the logic particle GA comes ONLY after a NAME.",
      "html": "remember, this GA is not the logic particle GA. THIS ONE comes after a VERB, the logic particle GA comes ONLY after a NAME.",
      "credits_raw": "Dario",
